ies  what we know is that most 2016 trump  voters are going to vote for trump again  what we know is that most 2016 hillary  voters are going to vote for biden  what we know is that independents are  leaning towards joe biden  and ultimately this is going to come  down to  who votes in which states and how much  of the vote can donald trump suppress  so maybe it's true that this particular  guy  was a lifelong democrat and he was  convinced after a life of voting for  democrats to vote for donald trump  because of kimberly guilfoyle screaming  on monday night at the republican  national convention  or as he says because the republican  convention kept mentioning god  the truth of course is that in reality  joe biden is more religious than donald  trump it's not something  i care about but for people who want a  religious candidate  there's no question that donald trump's  religiosity is completely fabricated and  fake  as something to appeal to evangelical  voters with trump as a politician  whereas joe biden actually seems to be a  moderate moderately devout catholic  i don't care about that but if you're  looking for the religious candidate it's  not donald trump it's joe biden  uh but sure the caller might be making  it up as well  it doesn't matter if we all go out and  vote period  and uh that is ultimately going to be  the one test it's not  did this guy switch in ohio by the way  ohio  not looking as good for joe biden as it  did before or i guess better said  looking better for donald trump recently  than it did before uh what matters is if  we all go out and vote and the large  numbers and so i wouldn't be lulled into  a false debate about whether it's  possible that the rnc  really shifted a democrat into voting  for trump i'm sure  some democrats did get convinced to vote  trump from the rnc  and some republicans were convinced to  vote for joe biden from the dnc  we're a country of 331 million the big  picture is what matters  let's not lose sight of tha